# Tests for the Dependents_benefit_split module

Run with `clerk test`. Each named scope is one concrete person, worked by
hand from IRC 152(e), Treas. Reg. § 1.152-4 and Pub. 501 (2024) pp 13-14,
17-18 as quoted in `catala/dependents_benefit_split.catala_en`. Every scope
sets satisfiable inputs (answers a real filer could give) and asserts the
expected result and the rejection of the wrong one. The oracle comparison is
`make difftest-persons` (per-person Direct File values, `oracle/persons.csv`).

> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as R
> Using Dependents_benefit_split as B

## Helper: a child of divorced parents with default answers

The default is the filer's biological son, born 2016-05-01 (8), a U.S.
citizen with an SSN, who lived with the filer all year. The filer (born
1985-06-15, not filing jointly) and the child's other parent are divorced;
the child was in their legal custody on July 2 and lived with them more than
six months; they paid over half of his support; there is no multiple support
agreement. The filer signed Form 8332 (`IDid`) and the child spent more
nights with the filer. The non-parent answers are "no". A test overrides
only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope MkMember:
  context relationship content Q.Relationship
  context date_of_birth content date
  context permanent_total_disability content boolean
  context which_parent content B.WrittenDeclaration
  context nights content B.NightsComparison
  context agi_higher content boolean
  context situation content B.ParentalSituation
  context parental_support content boolean
  context in_custody content boolean
  context parents_living content boolean
  context non_parental_signed content boolean
  context parents_meet_reqs content boolean
  context used_by_custodial_parent content boolean
  context special_agi content boolean
  context multiple_support_agreement content boolean
  output member content B.Member

scope MkMember:
  definition relationship equals Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
  definition date_of_birth equals |2016-05-01|
  definition permanent_total_disability equals false
  definition which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.IDid
  definition nights equals B.NightsComparison.More
  definition agi_higher equals false
  definition situation equals B.ParentalSituation.DivorcedOrSeparated
  definition parental_support equals true
  definition in_custody equals true
  definition parents_living equals false
  definition non_parental_signed equals false
  definition parents_meet_reqs equals false
  definition used_by_custodial_parent equals false
  definition special_agi equals false
  definition multiple_support_agreement equals false
  definition member equals B.Member {
    -- person: Q.Person {
         -- relationship: relationship
         -- date_of_birth: date_of_birth
         -- full_time_student: false
         -- permanent_total_disability: permanent_total_disability
         -- residency_duration: Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
         -- own_support: false
         -- married: false
         -- writable_joint_return: false
         -- writable_required_to_file: false
         -- writable_filing_only_for_refund: false
         -- writable_could_be_qualifying_child_of_another: false
         -- writable_potential_claimer_must_file: false
         -- writable_potential_claimer_did_file: false
         -- writable_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund: false }
    -- answers: B.BenefitSplitAnswers {
         -- has_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent: true
         -- non_parental_some_parent_not_claiming: non_parental_signed
         -- which_parent_not_claiming: which_parent
         -- in_parents_custody: in_custody
         -- lived_with_tp_or_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent_more_than_six_months:
              true
         -- biological_or_adoptive_parents_living: parents_living
         -- nights_with_tp_vs_other_parent: nights
         -- tp_agi_higher_than_other_parent: agi_higher
         -- parents_meet_reqs_rule_for_children_of_divorced_parents:
              parents_meet_reqs
         -- special_rule_child_used_by_custodial_parent_as_qp:
              used_by_custodial_parent
         -- special_rule_agi_test: special_agi
         -- parental_situation: situation
         -- parental_support: parental_support
         -- multiple_support_agreement: multiple_support_agreement }
  }
```

## The cases of issue #18

### More nights: the filer is the custodial parent, released the claim

Pub. 501 p 14, Example 1: "your child lived with you 210 nights and with the
other parent 156 nights. You are the custodial parent." The filer signed Form
8332, so the filer keeps HoH, EITC and CDCC (`tp_can_claim_split...`).
Known-bad output rejected: no knockout, and not "disqualified".

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMoreNightsCustodialReleased:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestMoreNightsCustodialReleased:
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion s.child_may_qualify_for_benefit_split
  assertion s.tp_is_parent and not s.tp_is_not_parent
  assertion s.parental_some_parent_not_claiming
  assertion s.primary_filer_not_claiming and not s.both_filers_not_claiming
  assertion not s.other_parent_not_claiming
  assertion not s.had_equal_number_of_nights_with_parents
  assertion s.parents_are_divorced_separated_or_living_apart
  assertion s.tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion not s.reached_non_parental_benefit_split
  assertion s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion not s.disqualified_due_to_parental_custody
  assertion not s.contradictory8832_knockout
  assertion not s.causes_noncustodial_parent_benefit_split_knockout
  assertion not s.unsupported
```

### Equal nights, higher AGI: the filer is the custodial parent

Treas. Reg. § 1.152-4(d)(4); Pub. 501 p 14, Example 3 (180 nights each, AGI
$40,000 against $25,000).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEqualNightsHigherAgi:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestEqualNightsHigherAgi:
  definition m.nights equals B.NightsComparison.Equal
  definition m.agi_higher equals true
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion s.had_equal_number_of_nights_with_parents
  assertion s.tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion not s.unsupported
```

### Equal nights, lower AGI: the other parent is custodial

The same child, but the filer's AGI is lower: the other parent is the
custodial parent, so the filer's "I signed" contradicts the rule that only
the custodial parent signs. Knocked out; known-bad output (custodial)
rejected.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEqualNightsLowerAgi:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestEqualNightsLowerAgi:
  definition m.nights equals B.NightsComparison.Equal
  definition m.agi_higher equals false
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion not s.tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion s.contradictory8832_tp_not_custodial_parent
  assertion s.contradictory8832_knockout
  assertion not s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion s.unsupported
```

### The custodial parent who released the claim keeps HoH, EITC and CDCC, not the dependent

Pub. 501 p 13: "only the noncustodial parent can: • Claim the child as a
dependent; and • Claim the child as a qualifying child for the child tax
credit, the credit for other dependents, or the additional child tax credit.
However, this doesn't allow the noncustodial parent to claim head of
household filing status, the credit for child and dependent care expenses,
... or the earned income credit."

This test wires this module's two outputs into
`Qualifying_relative.DependentTest` (the wiring listed in the PR): the child
is still the filer's qualifying child (HoH, EITC and CDCC read that, with
`tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc`), but is not an eligible or
claimed dependent, so there is no CTC, ACTC or ODC for him on this return.
Known-bad output rejected: `eligible_dependent` would be true without the
split.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCustodialReleasedKeepsHohEitcCdcc:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest
  internal d content R.DependentTest
  internal d_without_split content R.DependentTest
  internal answers content R.DependentAnswers

scope TestCustodialReleasedKeepsHohEitcCdcc:
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  definition answers equals R.DependentAnswers {
    -- gross_income: $0
    -- writable_qr_support_test: false
    -- tin_type: R.TinType.Ssn
    -- is_us_citizen_full_year: true
    -- writable_us_resident: false
    -- writable_us_national: false
    -- writable_canada_mexico_resident: false
    -- tp_claims: true
    -- tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc:
         s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
    -- disqualified_due_to_parental_custody:
         s.disqualified_due_to_parental_custody }
  definition d equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: R.Member { -- person: m.member.person -- answers: answers }
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  definition d_without_split equals
    output of R.DependentTest with {
      -- member: R.Member {
           -- person: m.member.person
           -- answers: answers but replace {
                -- tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc: false } }
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: false
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national: true }
  # Keeps HoH, EITC, CDCC
  assertion s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion d.qualifying_child
  # Not a dependent, so no CTC, ACTC or ODC
  assertion not d.eligible_dependent
  assertion not d.is_claimed_dependent
  assertion d.is_claimed_if_claimable
  # Without the release the same child is a claimed dependent
  assertion d_without_split.eligible_dependent
  assertion d_without_split.is_claimed_dependent
```

### Fewer nights, the other parent signed: noncustodial claimant, knocked out

The filer is the noncustodial parent holding a release: the child is the
filer's dependent under 152(e), a return DF does not support (scope.md 5.5).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNoncustodialClaimant:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestNoncustodialClaimant:
  definition m.nights equals B.NightsComparison.Less
  definition m.which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.TheyDid
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion s.other_parent_not_claiming
  assertion not s.tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion s.causes_noncustodial_parent_benefit_split_knockout
  assertion not s.contradictory8832_knockout
  assertion not s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion s.unsupported
```

### More nights, the other parent signed: contradictory, knocked out

Only the custodial parent signs (IRC 152(e)(2)(A)).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCustodialButOtherSigned:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestCustodialButOtherSigned:
  definition m.which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.TheyDid
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion s.tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion s.contradictory8832_tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion s.contradictory8832_knockout
  assertion not s.causes_noncustodial_parent_benefit_split_knockout
  assertion not s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion s.unsupported
```

### Nobody signed: no split

Treas. Reg. § 1.152-4(g) Example 2: "B does not execute a Form 8332 or
similar declaration ... Therefore, section 152(e) and this section do not
apply." On a joint return.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNobodySigned:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestNobodySigned:
  definition m.which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.NobodyDid
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: true }
  assertion s.tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion not s.parental_some_parent_not_claiming
  assertion not s.both_filers_not_claiming
  assertion not s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion not s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion not s.unsupported
```

### Parents together, the other parent signed: not divorced, no split

DF scenario `mfj-30k-eitc-ctc-actc`: the custodial filer says the other parent
signed, but the parental situation is "None of the above", so 152(e) does not
apply (152(e)(1)(A)) and the contradiction does not knock out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNotSeparatedNoKnockout:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestNotSeparatedNoKnockout:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.AdoptedChild
  definition m.which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.TheyDid
  definition m.situation equals B.ParentalSituation.Other
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: true }
  assertion s.tp_is_parent
  assertion not s.parents_are_divorced_separated_or_living_apart
  assertion s.contradictory8832_tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion not s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion not s.contradictory8832_knockout
  assertion not s.unsupported
```

### Custody ends at 18: born July 2, 2006, against July 3, 2006

Pub. 501 p 14, Example 5. A child who turns 18 on July 2, 2024 is in custody
183 of 366 nights, not more than half; one who turns 18 on July 3 is in
custody 184. Known-bad output rejected both ways.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAgeOfMajorityBoundary:
  m18 scope MkMember
  m17 scope MkMember
  internal s18 content B.BenefitSplitTest
  internal s17 content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestAgeOfMajorityBoundary:
  definition m18.date_of_birth equals |2006-07-02|
  definition m17.date_of_birth equals |2006-07-03|
  definition s18 equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m18.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  definition s17 equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m17.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion not s18.child_may_qualify_for_benefit_split
  assertion not s18.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion not s18.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion s17.child_may_qualify_for_benefit_split
  assertion s17.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion s17.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
```

### Permanently and totally disabled adult child

A 30-year-old disabled son still in his parents' legal custody (DF's
`childMayQualifyForBenefitSplit` second branch).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDisabledAdultChild:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestDisabledAdultChild:
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |1994-03-01|
  definition m.permanent_total_disability equals true
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1965-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion s.child_may_qualify_for_benefit_split
  assertion s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
```

### Multiple support agreement: the split does not apply (DF-BUG(18))

IRC 152(e)(5): "This subsection shall not apply in any case where over
one-half of the support of the child is treated as having been received from
a taxpayer under the provision of subsection (d)(3)." DF would split.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMultipleSupportAgreement:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestMultipleSupportAgreement:
  definition m.multiple_support_agreement equals true
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion not s.section_152e_applies_despite_support_agreements
  assertion s.tp_is_custodial_parent
  assertion not s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion not s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
```

### Grandparent, custodial parent not using the child, higher AGI

Pub. 501 p 17, Example 1 (Kody): the grandparent may use the child for HoH and
EITC; Kody is the other parent's dependent.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestGrandparentHigherAgi:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestGrandparentHigherAgi:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.GrandChildOrOtherDescendantOfChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2019-03-01|
  definition m.which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.NobodyDid
  definition m.parents_living equals true
  definition m.non_parental_signed equals true
  definition m.parents_meet_reqs equals true
  definition m.used_by_custodial_parent equals false
  definition m.special_agi equals true
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1960-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion s.tp_is_not_parent
  assertion s.reached_non_parental_benefit_split
  assertion s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion not s.disqualified_due_to_parental_custody
  assertion not s.unsupported
```

### Grandparent with lower AGI: disqualified

Pub. 501 p 18, Example 2: "Your parent can't claim Kody as a qualifying child
for any purpose because your parent's AGI isn't higher than yours."

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestGrandparentLowerAgi:
  m scope MkMember
  internal s content B.BenefitSplitTest

scope TestGrandparentLowerAgi:
  definition m.relationship equals Q.Relationship.GrandChildOrOtherDescendantOfChild
  definition m.date_of_birth equals |2019-03-01|
  definition m.which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.NobodyDid
  definition m.parents_living equals true
  definition m.non_parental_signed equals true
  definition m.parents_meet_reqs equals true
  definition m.special_agi equals false
  definition s equals
    output of B.BenefitSplitTest with {
      -- member: m.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1960-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion s.reached_non_parental_benefit_split
  assertion not s.eligible_for_benefit_split
  assertion not s.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  assertion s.disqualified_due_to_parental_custody
```

### Grandparent, the custodial parent uses the child: disqualified

Pub. 501 p 18, Example 3: the parent's claim wins.

```catala
