## The household

Two children: the first is the custodial-parent split above, the second a
noncustodial claim. The return is knocked out by the second only.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHousehold:
  first scope MkMember
  second scope MkMember
  internal h content B.BenefitSplit

scope TestHousehold:
  definition second.date_of_birth equals |2012-10-10|
  definition second.nights equals B.NightsComparison.Less
  definition second.which_parent equals B.WrittenDeclaration.TheyDid
  definition h equals
    output of B.BenefitSplit with {
      -- members: [first.member; second.member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion number of h.results = 2
  assertion not h.ko_knocked_out_by_contradictory8832
  assertion h.ko_knocked_out_by_non_custodial_parent_benefit_split
  assertion h.unsupported
```

The same household without the second child is supported.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHouseholdSupported:
  first scope MkMember
  internal h content B.BenefitSplit

scope TestHouseholdSupported:
  definition h equals
    output of B.BenefitSplit with {
      -- members: [first.member]
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: |1985-06-15|
      -- treat_as_mfj: false }
  assertion not h.ko_knocked_out_by_contradictory8832
  assertion not h.ko_knocked_out_by_non_custodial_parent_benefit_split
  assertion not h.unsupported
```
